# Files uploaded to Vercel are publicly fetchable. This repo has no
# buildCommand and no package.json scripts — Vercel serves it as static files
# plus api/*.ts as functions — so everything listed here is build-time or source
# material that was being served at 200 on steelwheellogistics.com until
# 2026-08-19. Verified before excluding: nothing in a served page references any
# of it, and api/*.ts only reads blog/posts.json, cities.json, and the three
# */pages.json manifests, none of which are excluded.
#
# If a buildCommand is ever added that runs the page generators, `scripts/` will
# have to come back out of this list.

# ── Page generators and maintenance scripts ─────────────────────────────────
# /scripts/build-transload-pages.js and friends were downloadable in full.
scripts/

# ── Tool build pipelines ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Python builders, the source CSVs behind the transload dataset, and scraped
# third-party PDFs/XLSX (EIA coal tables, USGS iron-ore surveys, an AAPA press
# archive). The CSVs in particular are the raw input to the directory — the
# data itself is the asset, and it was a public download.
tools/*/source/

# ── Raw scrapes and intermediate enrichment artifacts ───────────────────────
# This is the only data/ dir carrying more than its runtime JSON: raw scraped
# operator pages (a full 182KB Genesee & Wyoming page), enrichment .jsonl logs,
# probe/failure lists, and the superseded v1 transload.json. Keep ONLY the file
# the directory tool actually fetch()es.
tools/transload-directory/data/*
!tools/transload-directory/data/transload-v2.json
